# Commit and Push After Fixes

When you fix a bug, test failure, or CI issue in this repo:

1. Verify the fix (compile or run relevant tests when feasible).
2. Commit the change with a concise message focused on why.
3. Push to the current branch (`git push -u origin HEAD` if not tracking remote).

Do this without waiting for the user to ask — finishing a fix includes shipping it.

Do not commit unrelated untracked files (e.g. `samples/`) unless the user asked for them.
